    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "applicative",
        "title": "Doing it for someone: -ir- / -er-",
        "body": [
          "Add **-ir-** or **-er-** before the last vowel to say “for”, “to” or “at”: **-lima** (dig) becomes **-limira** (dig for), **-fumba** becomes **-fumbira** (cook for), **-tunda** becomes **-tundira** (sell at).",
          "Verbs with **e** or **o** in the stem usually take **-er-**: **-kola** becomes **-kolera** (work for), as in **Nkolera kampuni** from Unit 14."
        ],
        "table": [
          ["Verb", "For / to / at"],
          ["-lima (dig)", "-limira"],
          ["-fumba (cook)", "-fumbira"],
          ["-tunda (sell)", "-tundira"],
          ["-kola (work)", "-kolera"],
          ["-wandiika (write)", "-wandiikira"]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "The banana garden",
        "body": [
          "The **olusuku** (banana garden) is the centre of a Ganda homestead. Matooke grows all year round, and a well-kept olusuku was a sign of a good household."
        ]
      }
    ]
